                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Experienced on the Oculus Rift and Windows Mixed Reality[/h1]\n[i]Please note: I received a free Steam key through the Steam Curator Connect program.[/i]\n\nYou can view my review & gameplay here: https://youtu.be/JlNVDz56IzY\n\nIt's shocking that this game doesn't have more reviews. I know it came out during the Steam Summer sale, but this is one of better VR games. It's a good, challenging game. If you enjoy shoot 'em ups / bullet hells, this will be your jam. This game has a satisfying difficulty curve.\n\nAt first, I did seem impossible. However, you get used to the layout and enemy fire patterns. You get used to moving at high speeds forward, back, and side to side while aiming up and in front of your hoverbike, all while dancing away from each danger coming straight for you. I found each level or zone, got progressively more difficult and that made me have to get just that much better. \n\nYou can lower difficulty in the settings, however, I don't advise it. This is one of those games where you feel you are oh so close to beating the challenge, you just need one more try. Soon, what seemed impossible seems old hat and new challenges await that will further sharpen your skills.\n\nThe graphics are retro. I'm not going to sit here and tell you they look as good as Half-Life: Alyx because they simply don't. However, the good news is that the game did run smoothly for the most part on my 1060 GTX. You do have full locomotion on your hoverbike, there is no smooth or snap turning and it's not really needed in this game since most of the action is coming straight at you (although enemies will come from behind or from the sides so you do have to keep your head on a swivel). \n\nI did not experience any serious bugs, however, it did seem that the gun angle was slightly off on the Oculus Rift as I did have to aim a bit lower than usual to aim dead center. Unfortunately, on Windows Mixed Reality, motion controllers did not work by default and I did have to edit controller bindings within Steam VR to get it to work correctly. I hope that gets fixed soon and WMR official support is added.\n\n[b]Rate 7.5/10. Satisfying challenge. Highly recommended to fans of old school arcade shoot 'em ups / bullet hells. [/b]\n\n",
